# The rotor loop survives any number of effects at once (Paul's playtest, 2026-11-24: after the first
# drop-off the HQ's "saved" sound hung on and the v4 chop-chop never came back). Cause: ptplayer's
# automatic channel choice (PTPLAYER_SFX_CHANNEL_ANY) does not keep to sound.toml's sfx_channels when
# both effect channels are busy and the new effect is not of higher priority: it takes channel 2, the
# rotor's, and when the effect ends the channel loops ptplayer's idle word, not the rotor's wave.
# Ctrl+L, B plays three "saved" effects in one picture (the third has no free effect channel).
wait-serial "AGK t0" 1000
press fire 2
wait 125
mark idle
wait 30
mark idle_end
expect-sound idle idle_end
regs regs_before paula
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x35
wait 120
mark after
wait 60
mark after_end
regs regs_after paula
expect-serial "AGK sfx saved"
expect-sound after after_end
expect-serial "rotorPer=845 rotorHw=423 "
